      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OLE CHESTER (3) sets the standard after missing by only a neck behind Treacheroustimes at Shepparton in NR up to 44 grade, and he now drops to NR up to 37 with a better front-row draw. He also has recent head-to-head form over GLENBURNS WATERS and NIFTY SCHOOBEE, which strengthens his case. ARKLOW (2) comes off two plain Riverina Paceway efforts, but she was near the top of an open market last start, has proven Albury track-and-distance form and edged PEAKSART in that same race. PEAKSART (9) improved when third at West Wyalong, beaten just over nine metres, though the second-row draw is a genuine query and the recent matchups leave him with ground to make up on the top pair. NIFTY SCHOOBEE (1) drops from NR up to 44, has two wins and one placing from four attempts at this track and distance, and from the ace draw gets every chance to turn the recent plain form around.",
